# ============================================================================
# OnTrak — browser-console gateway (Apache Guacamole) environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` (never commit `.env`; it is gitignored) in this directory:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   docker compose up -d
#
# The portal signs every console connection; Guacamole only renders it. There is no
# Guacamole user database and no Guacamole login page a student ever sees — each
# session is handed a single-use, short-lived, encrypted payload scoped to exactly one
# machine.
#
# Secrets posture: in production this value comes from **Cerulean Vault**
# (`vault://ontrak/guacamole#json_secret_key`) and is resolved at deploy time.
# `.env` is local-only and carries either that reference or, where nothing resolves
# it, the resolved value.
# ============================================================================

# Must be exactly the same 32 hex characters as ONTRAK_GUAC__SECRET_KEY in the
# portal's environment (config: guac.secret_key). The portal signs with it and
# Guacamole verifies with it, so a mismatch shows up as "invalid login" in the
# console iframe and nothing else.
#
#   openssl rand -hex 16
JSON_SECRET_KEY=

# Where students' browsers reach the gateway. The portal's guac.base_url must match
# this exactly, including the trailing /guacamole/ path. Terminate TLS in front of
# this container: session payloads travel in a URL fragment and must not go over
# plain HTTP outside the host.
#   Public:  https://console.ontrak.innotel.us/guacamole/   (issued via Cerulean)
#   Local:   http://127.0.0.1:8080/guacamole/
PUBLIC_CONSOLE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/guacamole/
